vscode: select from after the paren to before the paren, carefully
open: format.ts

@brief
Eight times: `formatStatus` now takes the whole order. Replace both
arguments with `order`, save, quit.

Get inside the brackets, change what is in them, leave them standing.

@keys
| `f(` | onto the opening bracket |
| `ci(` | change everything between the pair |

@hints
The cursor has to be inside the brackets or on one of them — `ci(` does
not search forward for you.
--
`f(` then `ci(` then type `order`.

@solution
    f( ci( order <Esc> :wq<Enter>

Fifteen keystrokes.

`f(ci(` is one of the two or three sequences that separate someone who
knows the keys from someone who uses them. Argument lists change
constantly — a parameter added, a pair collapsed into an object, a call
site updated after a signature change — and every one of those edits is
this shape.

@start format.ts
export const label = formatStatus(order.status, order.locale);

@expected format.ts
export const label = formatStatus(order);
